WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:04.030
- It's not bad news, okay?

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:05.730
I do have something to tell you though.

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:08.630
We've been doing this for
three years and I mean,

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:09.630
I'm sure you've noticed,

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:11.950
I'm usually not in front of the camera,

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:13.800
and I mean, I did that for a reason,

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.850
I don't, I prefer to
stay behind the camera.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.810
Basically, what I'm trying to say

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.220
is that I'm doing something

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.460
that is completely
outside my comfort zone,

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:25.320
I'm starting a podcast and in the podcast

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:28.870
I'm always going to be in
them because I'm the host.

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:31.570
I've been wanting to start
a podcast for like two years

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:34.630
and just my fear of being in
front of the camera stopped me.

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:35.887
I get a lot of comments saying,

00:00:35.887 --> 00:00:37.920
"Thoraya, you should start a podcast.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:41.790
I love just listening to your
videos on my drive to work

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:43.540
or like when I'm doing laundry,

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:45.240
I just put my headphones in and I listen."

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.620
And I'm just like, "Dang,
I wish I wasn't so nervous

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:50.810
in front of the camera so I
could actually make a podcast."

00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:55.660
But that's what I'm doing now,
I'm getting over my fears.

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:56.530
Let me tell you why

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:58.820
it has been so hard for
me to start a podcast,

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:01.210
even though I've been wanting
to do it for two years.

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:02.610
Well, first of all, I'm the type of person

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:06.030
where if I wanna do something,
I just like do it right away.

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:09.110
This thing of like wanting to
do this and not being able to

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:11.750
it's been like eating away
at me for a really long time,

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:14.170
so I just got to the
point where I don't know,

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:16.970
I was just like, "I preach
this whole being-bold thing,

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:19.890
why can't I just be a
little bold and do this?"

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.480
But yeah, let me get back to why

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:23.300
it's so hard to do a podcast.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:26.820
I'm a pretty shy person,

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.360
until you get to know me, of course,

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:30.387
but like, when people tell me like,

00:01:30.387 --> 00:01:32.680
"Wow you must be so outgoing,
you meet so many people."

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:36.330
I just think to myself, "Little
do you know." (chuckles)

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:37.930
But the thing is like,

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:40.250
when you have a passion for something

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:42.470
you're willing to like grind through

00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:43.730
things that hold you back.

00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:45.610
I rely heavily on skills

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:48.660
that I've just practiced
over and over again,

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:52.290
I've just always felt
like to be a podcast host,

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:54.600
you just have to be like naturally gifted

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:58.410
and able to ignore the camera

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:01.230
and the fact that you're being recorded.

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:03.680
And if the person for example,

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:06.580
my worst fear is like to have a guest on

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:08.650
who says the most amazing story

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:10.720
and I just reply in a really dumb way

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:15.010
and I'm just like, "Do I put
this episode up and look dumb?

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:18.800
Or do I not put it up and
just lose this amazing story?"

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:23.050
So I don't know, it's just,
it's been a lot of overthinking

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:25.300
and a lot of fear that's
been holding me back

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:28.720
but obviously we're here
because I finally did it,

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:30.300
that's the good news. (chuckles)

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.690
I do wanna warn you guys though,

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:35.890
this is something where
I'm learning as I go,

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:38.870
like I could've just
like practiced on my own

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:40.010
for a really long time,

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:42.000
gotten really good at
it and then launched it,

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:46.190
but I just thought it would
be cool to get your feedback

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:48.410
as I look super awkward
in front of the camera

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:49.630
and like, I don't know,

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:52.870
I guess it'll be fun to look
back on my first episode,

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:54.630
once we're like 100 episodes in.

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:56.810
I've been trying to figure
out a way to announce it

00:02:56.810 --> 00:03:01.810
and I thought, why not
just do what I'm best at?

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:06.420
Being in front of the camera,
that's sarcasm. (chuckles)

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:09.740
And I don't know what it is
about you guys, honestly,

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:12.060
like you just have some sort of magic.

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:13.740
I know a lot of people say this,

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:15.250
that they have the best subscribers,

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:19.700
but I'm like, I think I'm
being completely unbiased

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:23.010
when I say that, "No, I
have the best subscribers."

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:26.040
I'm still a hot mess, but I
was even more of a hot mess

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:30.540
before you guys, so let
me thank you for that,

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:33.060
but I'm saying all of this to say

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:36.270
that I know how powerful
your kindness can be

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:39.880
because I've lived it firsthand
for the past three years

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:43.700
and I guess what I'm trying to ask is

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:46.450
whatever magic it is that you guys do

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:48.640
and have done from my YouTube channel,

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:52.470
I hope you'll consider
also working that magic

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:56.350
for my podcast, 'cause I do
wanna give it a solid shot,

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:59.010
I don't wanna do it, see
that it's not going so well

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:00.660
and kind of give up on the idea.

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:04.220
And I know that the only way
I could give it a solid shot

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:07.050
is if we all go into it together.

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:08.880
I don't want to half-ass it,

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:11.380
I want to see if we can actually do it.

00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:13.440
So if you don't mind,

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:16.380
I'm going to list a few
things that you could do

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:18.870
to best help launch my podcast.

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:20.920
It's going to launch January 12th

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:22.790
and I guess the first step is, listen?

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:25.650
Hopefully you'll love
it, but if you hate it,

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:28.480
please let me know in
private that you hate it,

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:33.480
because I might be a little
fragile the first few episodes,

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.947
but if you love it and
you think to yourself,

00:04:35.947 --> 00:04:38.270
"You know what, I'm gonna work my magic."

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:41.240
Then, these are the things
that will help most.

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:45.630
First, leave a five-star
review on Apple Podcasts.

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:47.290
I don't know why this is so important

00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:49.017
but everyone keeps telling me like,

00:04:49.017 --> 00:04:51.130
"Tell people to leave
you a five-star review."

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:54.080
The podcast is gonna be
available everywhere, basically,

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:57.810
like Spotify, Anchor, Google
Podcasts and a lot of others

00:04:57.810 --> 00:05:00.640
and of course, following and
subscribing on them will help,

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:02.080
but the most important thing,

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:02.930
it's really important

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:05.890
to get a lot of five-star
reviews on Apple Podcasts

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:07.920
and so I thought we would
have some fun with it.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:09.570
If you decide to leave a five-star review,

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:12.540
I thought it would be cool for
you to answer this question,

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:15.250
who's one stranger you still remember?

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:18.580
So under a five-star
review on Apple Podcasts,

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:21.940
answer the question, who's one
stranger you still remember?

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:24.410
I'll read through every
single one, I promise.

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:25.960
Even if there are 10,000,

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:27.560
I'm gonna read through every single one.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:30.310
I'm gonna choose some to
share on my Instagram Story,

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:31.950
so leave your Instagram handle as well

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:33.070
if you want me to tag you

00:05:33.070 --> 00:05:35.820
and of course, obviously
subscribing and following

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:37.620
on whatever platform you listen on

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:39.860
or all of them if you wanna go all out.

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:42.360
And even though the podcast
launches on the 12th

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:45.120
I actually have my trailer
and my profile up now,

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:47.260
so you can start doing
all these things today.

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:48.290
I'll make sure to have

00:05:48.290 --> 00:05:50.430
my podcast's links in the description.

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:51.790
Another thing I think would really help

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:53.870
is to share the podcast

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:55.670
with someone you think would love it.

00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:57.040
So if you listen to the podcast

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:59.840
and it makes you think of
someone you think would love it,

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:00.750
send it to them.

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:04.450
For every episode, every single
one, just send it to people.

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:06.190
We're gonna learn as we go.

00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:07.590
We're gonna grow as we go

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:11.420
and how sick would it be if
we made like the top charts?

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:12.330
Can you imagine?

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:13.290
Oh my God.

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:17.990
I don't really have any, like, goals.

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:18.823
I don't know.

00:06:19.666 --> 00:06:21.680
I mean, it would to make
like the top charts,

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:23.820
but I feel that's just so out there,

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:26.780
I don't even know if that's possible

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:30.440
but I guess that could be a goal.

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:31.273
Okay, you know what?

00:06:31.273 --> 00:06:33.010
When I had 300 subscribers

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:34.750
I made it a goal to hit a million

00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:36.850
and I thought it was
impossible at the time.

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:39.070
So let's do the same again right now.

00:06:39.070 --> 00:06:41.480
Obviously, it's not about the numbers,

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:45.940
but as a creator, it is
cool to get more people

00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:48.560
to see what you make,
to hear what you make,

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:50.519
so I try to limit the amount of times

00:06:50.519 --> 00:06:52.440
I put number goals out there

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:55.090
but it is fun to do every once in a while

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:56.447
just so you can look back and be like,

00:06:56.447 --> 00:06:59.100
"Oh my gosh, I can't
believe that happened."

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:02.410
And also I'll be posting
the video version on the,

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:04.600
I didn't even tell you guys
what the podcast is about,

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:05.500
oh my God.

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:06.950
Okay, do you wanna know?

00:07:06.950 --> 00:07:09.030
Let me tell you what the podcast is about.

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:10.950
It's actually super exciting.

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:12.670
Okay, I want the podcast to be

00:07:12.670 --> 00:07:14.890
a podcast version of my channel

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:17.350
and how I thought was best to do this

00:07:17.350 --> 00:07:21.300
is for me to set up two
chairs, two microphones,

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:23.660
and two cameras, of course, in public,

00:07:23.660 --> 00:07:25.220
on sidewalks, at parks.

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:28.160
I sit on one chair and the
other chair is for my guest

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:32.090
who has to be a stranger that
I meet on the spot that day,

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:33.050
I get them in the chair

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:34.590
and I have them answer

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:36.370
the questions you've seen on my channel,

00:07:36.370 --> 00:07:38.240
I get them to tell me their secrets,

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:40.150
I get them to do something bold

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:42.000
like maybe call their crush.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:43.630
And I guess the only difference

00:07:43.630 --> 00:07:45.380
between my podcast and my channel

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:49.180
is that you get to know these
strangers on a deeper level.

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:52.260
I didn't think that was
possible, but it turns out it is.

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:53.590
For example, on my channel,

00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:56.210
you see like 30 strangers per episode

00:07:56.210 --> 00:08:00.200
and at most maybe one of their
segments is two minutes long.

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:02.920
So now just imagine that one stranger

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:05.100
who has a two-minute segment on my episode

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:06.920
now has an entire hour.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:08.890
I know you'll fall in
love with these people

00:08:08.890 --> 00:08:13.070
because I've been falling in
love with them and their story.

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:17.060
It's just been like a shift
in the way I do things.

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:19.820
Before, I would just meet
someone for a couple of minutes,

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:22.330
maybe we'd talk for like 5
to 10 minutes off camera,

00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:24.940
if they were willing,
but this is just like,

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:28.010
I've become friends with
almost every single person

00:08:28.010 --> 00:08:31.820
who I've interviewed so far,
so it's been pretty cool.

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:34.940
And another cool thing is
I'll have follow-up episodes,

00:08:34.940 --> 00:08:36.730
I'm sure you guys will,

00:08:36.730 --> 00:08:38.580
based on the stories I've heard so far,

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:40.400
you guys are gonna want
to know follow-ups.

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:42.740
Other things I'm considering
doing for the podcast

00:08:42.740 --> 00:08:45.230
is this thing called Thoraya's voicemail.

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:46.830
If you guys follow me on Instagram,

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:49.420
you'll see that I have
this number you can call in

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:51.640
and leave a secret for my voicemail

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:54.170
and this might be like bonus audio

00:08:54.170 --> 00:08:55.490
at the end of each episode,

00:08:55.490 --> 00:08:56.920
but I'll play basically,

00:08:56.920 --> 00:08:59.800
a bunch of voicemails from
you guys sharing your secrets.

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:02.330
There's just so many,
there's so much I wanna do

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:04.810
and I think the more I overcome my fears,

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:09.210
the more freedom I'll
have to be able to do this

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:12.050
and that's really exciting
and nerve-racking.

00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:14.740
It's like a mixture of
such opposite feelings,

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:16.990
I'm super excited but super nervous,

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:21.290
super stressed but super
anxious in a good way,

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:22.470
I don't know, it just,

00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:24.250
it's been an interesting couple of months

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:26.660
leading up to this, but
yeah, that's what it's about.

00:09:26.660 --> 00:09:28.900
I mean, this video is
really all over the place,

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:31.720
if you're still here,
thank you. (chuckles)

00:09:31.720 --> 00:09:35.000
I think that's it, I think
that's all I wanted to say.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:35.850
Did I even tell you?

00:09:35.850 --> 00:09:38.540
I didn't even tell you guys
what it's called, oh my God.

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:41.360
This is the worst announcement video ever.

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:43.650
The podcast is called, oh my gosh,

00:09:43.650 --> 00:09:47.130
the podcast is called, how
perfect I have it right here.

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:50.370
Okay, so here is the big reveal.

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:52.540
I didn't even plan on
having this be a big reveal,

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:54.400
it was just 'cause I forgot
to tell you, (chuckles)

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:55.660
but now it's a big reveal.

00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:56.850
I'm gonna reveal the name

00:09:56.850 --> 00:09:59.250
but let me go over all
these things one more time.

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:01.540
January 12th, the podcast
is going to launch,

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:03.830
each episode will air every Tuesday.

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:06.130
The video version will
air a few days later

00:10:06.130 --> 00:10:07.660
on my YouTube channel.

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:09.510
Listen to the podcast first,

00:10:09.510 --> 00:10:12.130
try to imagine what you
think the guests look like

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:14.480
and then come on my YouTube channel

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:16.240
maybe before you watch the video,

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:18.360
leave a comment guessing what you think

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:19.440
that they would look like,

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:21.610
share the podcast with your friends

00:10:21.610 --> 00:10:24.260
and then obviously, the
most important thing,

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:26.940
leave a five-star review
on Apple Podcasts.

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:29.010
I'll make sure to link
everything in the description.

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:32.200
Okay, so now for the big reveal.

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:34.470
I'll reveal the name and we'll end this

00:10:34.470 --> 00:10:37.050
with a preview of the podcast.

00:10:37.050 --> 00:10:42.050
The podcast is going to
be called "Hey, Stranger!"

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:43.970
Is that in focus?

00:10:43.970 --> 00:10:44.990
There it is.

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:47.480
That's pretty much it, thank
you guys for everything,

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:51.270
I love you so much and
we'll meet on January 12th,

00:10:51.270 --> 00:10:54.142
the day my podcast launches.

00:10:54.142 --> 00:10:54.975
(clapperboard snaps)

00:10:54.975 --> 00:10:56.447
(gentle music)

00:10:56.447 --> 00:10:59.477
"Hey, Stranger!" (chuckles)

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:06.700
Hello to everyone listening.

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:10.180
My name is Thoraya, this is
the "Hey, Stranger!" podcast

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:12.910
and before we start, let
me set the scene for you.

00:11:12.910 --> 00:11:15.090
I'm currently sitting in
a chair at my local park

00:11:15.090 --> 00:11:16.450
which also happens to be

00:11:16.450 --> 00:11:19.260
one of the biggest tourist
attractions in my city.

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:20.780
Across from me is an empty chair

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:23.290
and on today's and every episode

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:25.340
that empty chair will be filled one by one

00:11:25.340 --> 00:11:27.070
by people of different backgrounds,

00:11:27.070 --> 00:11:29.070
mindsets and walks of life.

00:11:29.070 --> 00:11:33.211
The only criteria is
that they are a stranger.

00:11:33.211 --> 00:11:35.794
(joyful music)

